      "title": "Note",
      "properties": {},
      "widgets_values": [
        "# Krea 2 Turbo \u2014 image to image (masked add-an-object)\n\n**Matched set (change one, change all five):**\n\n| slot | value |\n|---|---|\n| diffusion model | `krea2TurboFP8_krea2TURBO.safetensors` |\n| text encoder | `qwen3vl_4b_bf16.safetensors` \u2014 `CLIPLoader type = **krea2**` |\n| VAE | `qwen_image_vae.safetensors` |\n| latent | from `VAEEncode` (16-ch) |\n| patch node | **none** \u2014 Krea 2 has no `ModelSampling*` and no `FluxGuidance` |\n\n`type=krea2` is not guessable: an unknown string silently falls back to CLIP-L\nand fails much later with a shape error.\n\n**Turbo is guidance-distilled \u21d2 CFG stays at 1.0.** The negative branch is never\nevaluated at CFG 1.0, which is why the negative prompt runs through\n`ConditioningZeroOut` instead of carrying text. Raising CFG degrades output.\n\n### This is the top-hat workflow\n\nKrea 2 Turbo is a **plain text-to-image model** \u2014 there is no Krea 2 inpaint\ncheckpoint and no edit conditioning to load. So the edit is done the\nmodel-agnostic way: `SetLatentNoiseMask` tells the sampler *\"only these latent\ncells are yours; re-paste the original everywhere else after every step.\"*\nThe model still sees the whole latent each step, so it grows a hat that matches\nthe dog's lighting and perspective instead of a floating sticker.\n\n### Do this, in order\n\n1. Drop the photo at\n   `/home/bdgr/Models/ComfyUI-next/input/example_dog.png`\n   (or just click **choose file to upload** on the Source image node).\n2. Hit **Queue**. Look at the red overlay in **Mask preview** first \u2014 that red\n   box is exactly where the hat will be drawn.\n3. Nudge `location_x / location_y / shape_width / shape_height` on **Hat region**\n   until the box sits above the head with its lower edge overlapping the skull.\n   Coordinates are in the resized 832x1248 frame, origin top-left,\n   `location_*` is the **centre** of the box.\n4. Re-queue.\n\n**The box must overlap the head.** A box floating in empty space above the dog\ngives the model no anchor and you get a hat in mid-air.\n\n### Painted mask instead\nRight-click Source image \u2192 **Open in MaskEditor**, paint the hat area, save,\nthen drag `LoadImage`'s **MASK** output onto **Feather the seam**'s `mask` input.\nThat replaces the rectangle. Everything downstream is unchanged.\n\n### If the hat does not blend\n- raise `blur_radius` on **Feather the seam** (24 \u2192 40) for a softer seam\n- raise `expand` to give the model more room to draw the brim\n- drop KSampler `denoise` to `0.85` so a ghost of the original guides it\n- re-roll `seed` \u2014 a 10-step turbo model is genuinely seed-sensitive here\n"
      ],
      "color": "#432",
      "bgcolor": "#653"
    },
